        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "99472cc8-85b1-3a8e-916d-201658ecc5d4",
                "word": "obliquity",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8a50d676-2a8f-4675-9d5e-119c7abf61a9",
                        "entry_id": "99472cc8-85b1-3a8e-916d-201658ecc5d4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "obliquities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f93842f8-a762-30e8-8def-6c2b3bbc6082",
                        "entry_id": "99472cc8-85b1-3a8e-916d-201658ecc5d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obliquité, inclinaison d’une ligne, d’une surface sur une autre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Depuis le XVᵉ siècle"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cdb83f0-4ddc-4468-9f8a-daf8a0751526",
                                "sense_id": "f93842f8-a762-30e8-8def-6c2b3bbc6082",
                                "text": "The Planet Earth, so stedfast though she seem, / Insensibly three different Motions move? / Which else to several Sphears thou must ascribe, / Mov’d contrarie with thwart obliquities"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d38167a-b12f-4a2a-a3c7-227eefcbc6c1",
                                "sense_id": "f93842f8-a762-30e8-8def-6c2b3bbc6082",
                                "text": "She wore glasses which, in humble reference to a divergent obliquity of vision, she called her straighteners, and a little ugly snuff-coloured dress trimmed with satin bands in the form of scallops and glazed with antiquity."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d4143f21-6080-36c1-bb0e-491590363d7d",
                        "entry_id": "99472cc8-85b1-3a8e-916d-201658ecc5d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obliquité, ce qu’il y a de contraire à la droiture, à la franchise dans sa conduite, dans ses démarches, dans ses comportements."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Depuis le XVᵉ siècle"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9a9caa0-1031-4405-bcca-04ffb76e2152",
                                "sense_id": "d4143f21-6080-36c1-bb0e-491590363d7d",
                                "text": "Habitually living with the elements and knowing little more of the land than as a beach, or, rather, that portion of the terraqueous globe providentially set apart for dance-houses, doxies and tapsters, in short what sailors call a \"fiddlers'-green,\" his simple nature remained unsophisticated by those moral obliquities which are not in every case incompatible with that manufacturable thing known as respectability."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da6b5ca0-d585-4422-b3b4-58efc829c998",
                                "sense_id": "d4143f21-6080-36c1-bb0e-491590363d7d",
                                "text": "Stray’s [friends], apt to keep more to the shadows, tended to be practitioners of obliquity—as it quite often came down to, varieties of pimp."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1291eea1-75f9-4a0a-bfc1-354f8b0a8b61",
                                "sense_id": "d4143f21-6080-36c1-bb0e-491590363d7d",
                                "text": "That spiked my gun. I could not say anything. I was entirely out of verbal obliquities; to go further would be to lie, and that I would not do; so I simply sat still and suffered , -- sat mutely and resignedly there, and sizzled, -- for I was being slowly fried to death in my own blushes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
